# Environment variables. Copy to `.env` for local work, or paste the values into
# Vercel under Settings -> Environment Variables. `.env` is gitignored, this file
# is not, so the shape of what is needed can be committed without the values.
#
# Nothing here is required for the site to work.
#
# The viewer badge hides itself and the endpoint returns 503 when these are
# absent, which is the intended failure: a portfolio should not show an error
# because a counter is not configured. Everything else - all nine sections, the
# resume, the chat - is static and needs no backend at all.

# --- presence badge (/api/viewers) ------------------------------------------
#
# These are the variable names Vercel's own Redis Marketplace integration
# creates, so installing that integration is enough and no values need pasting.
# If you would rather use Upstash directly, both names still work; use your own
# REST endpoint and token in their place.
#
#   Vercel:    Storage -> Create -> Redis
#   Upstash:   console.upstash.com -> Database -> REST API

KV_REST_API_URL=https://your-database.upstash.io
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=your-rest-token